he's David Ayres the Hurricanes  emergency goalie got the wind the ripe  old age of 42 David how you feeling  today a little tired I feel good all  right if I told you a week ago hey by  the way you're gonna make your NHL debut  coming up in a week and you're not going  to be playing for Toronto the team that  employs you you're gonna be playing for  the Carolina Hurricanes what would you  say I would say I'll take that any day  you know just a chance to get out on the  ice and make a couple saves it doesn't  matter who who it is I would love to get  out there but the Hurricanes were  fantastic these guys were amazing  everybody that I've met in the  organization it's been unreal and I'm  excited to get to rally to see you bunch  of the guys and watch a game okay but  I'm just trying to understand trying to  wrap my head around it the home team has  to have that emergency backup to the  backup goaltender and that's you so you  could have played for Toronto if there  were injuries now you're going against  Toronto and you're gonna play for  Carolina and then you let the first two  goals in and I thought oh no you can't  have this he's he's employed by Toronto  what did he did any of the players say  hey David at least go through the  motions here act like a goalie this is  not cool you know we kind of want to  smack myself upside the head and wake up  a little bit but the players were good  they just came up to me and said relax  and take it easy and mate just you know  have fun make some saves and they played  great in front of me and we ended up  pulling through in the third period and  a good win but you're not the Maple  Leafs Zamboni driver you haven't  graduated to that you're right you're  the AHL did the Toronto Marlies you're  their Zamboni driver yeah so I've driven  four leaves before a few years back and  I actually haven't driven for the  Marley's in the past five five and a  half years so the whole Zamboni thing is  kind of old now I I Drive maybe once 